    "summary": {
      "en": "Dantidurga's Malwa expedition: after the death of his Chalukya overlord in 747 the Rashtrakuta Dantidurga marched north, extinguished the Gurjara kingdom of Nandipuri in southern Gujarat, and proclaimed the conquest of Malwa by performing the Hiranyagarbha-dana ceremony at its capital Ujjayini, where the defeated Gurjara king is said to have served him as door-keeper. The victory was not followed by annexation: Nagabhata I was still acknowledged as suzerain at Broach in 756 and left a kingdom in Malwa and Rajputana to his successors.",
      "kn": ""
    },
    "participants": [],
