    "summary": {
      "en": "Mahmud of Lahore's raid on Kannauj and Kalanjara: after the deaths of Bhoja and Karna removed the two princes who had frightened the Ghaznavids out of Hindustan for half a century, Ibrahim's son Mahmud, governor of the Punjab, drove into the Doab some time between 1086 and 1090. He plundered Kannauj and Kalanjara and invaded Ujjain, took Agra by defeating its chief Jaipal, and found an ally in Kannauj named Chand Rai — HCIP identifies him with Chandradeva, the founder of Gahadavala power, who seized the throne of Kannauj from the Rashtrakuta Gopala in the disorder that followed Mahmud's departure. At Kalanjara the Chandella Kirttivarman fought Mahmud off successfully.",
      "kn": ""
    },
