    "route": null,
    "summary": {
      "en": "Vikramaditya VI burns Vengi: some time between 1091 and 1093 the Chalukya emperor and his general Govindarasa burnt Vengi and defeated the Velananti chief Gonka I, and Chalukya records claim that the Andhra country was wrested from Vira-Choda, son of Kulottunga I. The raid did not change who governed the province. Kulottunga's sons held the Vengi viceroyalty without a break — Vira-Choda to 1092, then his brother Vikrama Chola from 1092 to 1118 — which is why the map does not move here. Vikramaditya VI's object of separating the Eastern Chalukya and Chola crowns was achieved only at the end of his reign, when Vengi passed to him in 1118.",
      "kn": ""
    },
