    "polityName": "Seuna (Yadava)",
    "date": {
      "from": 1050,
      "to": 1068,
      "era": "CE",
      "precision": "range"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "A feudatory Seuna, not an independent king. The Struggle for Empire (HCIP V), p. 167: 'Bhillama III of the Yadava dynasty of Seuna-desa, who married the daughter of Jayasimha II' of the Chalukyas of Kalyana; he was defeated by Jayasimha II's officer Bijjarasa. Sastri, A History of South India (genealogical table, block 180), enters Avalladevi, sister of Somesvara I (1042-68), as married to 'Seuna Bhillama III'. Dates approximate - no regnal years of his own survive and the span is a bracket.",
      "kn": ""
    },
    "citations": [],
